# Branch-local bindings do not escape

Verifies `if` and `else` blocks are independent child scopes. The same name may
be declared in each, but neither binding is visible after the conditional.

>>> source
if (true) {
    let x: int = 10
    print(x)
} else {
    let x: int = 20
}

print(x)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: unknown binding `x` at Span { start: 83, end: 84 }

<<< exit
1
